{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Give victims the right to view a recent photograph of their convicted offender",
        "additional_details": "Victims can lose so much control through crime and the justice process. Some never want to see their offender again; others need to know what they look like. Current decisions can focus on risk management or approaching release. Victims should have greater choice throughout a sentence, including for reassurance and reducing uncertainty. A recent photo could be viewed privately and securely, without providing a copy, with appropriate safeguards.",
        "background": "Give victims of serious sexual and violent offences the right to request to privately view a recent photograph of their convicted offender during their custodial sentence, with appropriate safeguards. Victim choice should matter, not only immediate risk or proximity to release.",
